    {
      "id": "claim_752f10b729cf4e51b6ed19a2a684d501",
      "statement": "ChatModelProvider.createChatModel() exhaustively switches over ChatModelPlatform (OPENAI, OLLAMA, BLABLADOR, DEEPSEEK, OPENWEBUI, BIFROST) and delegates to private per-platform factories that each return a LazyChatModel, so no branch constructs a platform client directly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/llm/chat/ChatModelProvider.java#L117-L124",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f1dfe74e3586694aac2b7dc905dbe5b354587133a3e269cc2e1545698dcffaed:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_20655cb3e3df42b9b49796022026998c",
      "statement": "The per-platform factories resolve environment variables eagerly inside createChatModel() — required ones via EnvironmentProvider.getenvNonNull (IllegalStateException when unset) and optional ones via getenv — while the LangChain4j client is constructed only by the supplier on the first chat call, so missing credentials fail fast at factory time and client/connection errors surface at first use.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/llm/chat/ChatModelProvider.java#L171-L187",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1db8db0b8c42b8923aea9b15001cc711e61e44a0e13dc0a103e4c84b65523f39:"
